# Optional. Nothing here is needed to run AdmitPerf against a local engine,
# or to deploy an ungated model to Modal after `modal setup`.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is read by every `admitperf` command, including the ones the dashboard
# runs for you. Anything already exported wins, so a one-off
# `HF_TOKEN=... admitperf infra up` still overrides the file.

# Gated weights only (Llama, Gemma). Forwarded to the container at deploy time
# as a Modal secret; never written into an image layer.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx

# Alternative to the above, if you would rather keep the token in Modal:
#   modal secret create huggingface HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# ADMITPERF_HF_SECRET=huggingface

# Modal auth, if you cannot run `modal setup` interactively (CI).
# MODAL_TOKEN_ID=ak-...
# MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=as-...

# NOT USED YET. There is no Lambda provider — `infra up` only supports Modal.
# To benchmark against a Lambda box you start yourself, skip provisioning:
#   admitperf run --policy kv_threshold --engine-url http://<host>:8000
# LAMBDA_HOST=ubuntu@1.2.3.4
# LAMBDA_SSH_KEY=~/.ssh/id_ed25519_lambda
